llvm-3.7.1 forward port: a store of a floating-point constant becomes an integer store only after the merge attempt

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for consecutive stores of constants
where some are floating-point: 3.7.1's DAGCombiner::visitSTORE turns
`store float C` into `store i32 bits(C)` before it tries
MergeConsecutiveStores, so which stores are still floating-point when their
neighbour is visited depends on visit order and a run merges in the wrong
pairs. The base merges the floats of a run with each other: an int 0, a
float 0 and a float 0 at +0x30, +0x34, +0x38 are `mov dword [rsi + 0x30], 0`
then one 8-byte store (0xe903a0; 3.7.1's object merges the int with the
first float); three float zeros are an 8-byte store then a 4-byte one
(0x57fc10; 3.7.1's object has the 4-byte one first).

Three upstream commits, each whole (tests left out), first released in
3.8.0, applied with offsets (fuzz 3 and 1 on two hunks of the first):
  r248168 (a30ddb652419, 2015-09-21) "Factor replacement of stores of FP
    constants into new function": the block of visitSTORE becomes
    replaceStoreOfFPConstant, no change of behaviour;
  r248169 (b77483442943, 2015-09-21) "DAGCombiner: Replace store of FP
    constant after attemping store merges": the call moves below the merge
    attempt: the change itself;
  r248190 (8fb9b94f7f0d, 2015-09-21) "Fix accidentally committed debug
    printing": removes the dbgs() lines r248168 left in the new function.

Swept alone over the game module built by the installed 3.7.1 (round 273B,
5,496 rows, 6,656 functions): 3 functions change; the 3 rows become equal
(5,297 to 5,300: 0x57fc10, 0xe903a0, and 0xacd590, whose 8-byte store
is the pair at +0x18 and not the pair at +0x1c) and none is lost.

